      "assumptions": [
        "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero as an explicit extension of the source Euclidean setting. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and βη≤1. Set μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd. Let P be the actual conditional-expectation orthogonal projection onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra in L²(J). ",
        "Centering and macro range restrict the conclusion input; no supplied operator/law/onto/root certificate.",
        "Base finite dimension does not imply finite-dimensional L2; rank zero is explicitly extended."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero as an explicit extension of the source Euclidean setting. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and βη≤1. Set μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd. Let P be the actual conditional-expectation orthogonal projection onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra in L²(J). There exists one linear isometry U:L²(J)→L²(J) whose AE representative is composition with F(x,y)=(x,2x−y), with U²=I and U self-adjoint. Define A=PUP and B=(I−P)UP. For every f∈ran P with ∫f dJ=0, ‖Af‖≤[(1−αη)/(1+αη)]‖f‖ and [4αη/(1+αη)²]‖f‖²≤‖Bf‖². This includes αη=1, uses the actual, potentially infinite-dimensional L²(J), without imposing finite-dimensionality on L², and is Test-level integration of already produced operators; Γ, its inverse and trajectories are not asserted.",
      "formula": "\\rho=\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta},\\quad\\|Af\\|\\le\\rho\\|f\\|,\\quad\\|Bf\\|^2\\ge\\frac{4\\alpha\\eta}{(1+\\alpha\\eta)^2}\\|f\\|^2\\quad(f\\in\\operatorname{ran}P\\cap L^2_0(J)).",
      "boundary": "PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5 exact macro identification/centering feeding C3-C4 and B15. Public actual canonical pullback range=P range and centered image equality; real new Test transports exact57 scalar contraction to all actual centered macro f and squared defect gap. Finite real Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicit extension; trueL2 generally infinite dimensional. Public generic pullback range and actual PBPS range/mean/centered image; realTest-only allmacro contraction/squaredBgap. NoGamma/fullweakH1/B13/B14/dynamics/main/cost/composition/fullpaper/Goal claim.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Match the actual previously produced operators",
          "text": "The actual reflection/mean theorem produces U,M55,T55 and its defect identity. AE canonical pullback shows M55=M. AE equality to the same literal reflected kernel S, whose every-y density is produced internally, gives T55=T57 for the already verified sharp scalar contraction operator.",
          "formula": "M_{55}=M,\\quad T_{55}=T_{57},\\quad MT_{55}=AM.",
          "lean": "L2MacroscopicMean.actual_macroscopic_l2_mean; hSameM; hSd; hLaw; hSameT; Tests.GaussianMarginalPoincare.actual_same_mean_centered_contraction"
        },
        {
          "title": "Lift scalar contraction to every macro input",
          "text": "The new full centered image produces centered u with Mu=f for every centered f in ranP. Apply the verified exact scalar contraction to this same T55, then use MT55=AM and isometry of M. No caller image or output-centering certificate is used.",
          "formula": "f=Mu,\\quad\\|Af\\|=\\|MTu\\|=\\|Tu\\|\\le\\rho\\|u\\|=\\rho\\|f\\|.",
          "lean": "MacroscopicRange.actual_macroscopic_centered_range; hCentered; hCon; hMT; M.norm_map"
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive the sharp squared defect gap",
          "text": "The actual orthogonal norm defect is ‖BMu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². Original α≤β and βη≤1 imply 0≤αη≤1 and ρ≥0, so the norm contraction can be squared. Subtraction and exact scalar algebra give 1−ρ²=4αη/(1+αη)², without division by 1−αη.",
          "formula": "\\|Bf\\|^2=\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2\\ge(1-\\rho^2)\\|u\\|^2=\\frac{4\\alpha\\eta}{(1+\\alpha\\eta)^2}\\|f\\|^2.",
          "lean": "hDef; ha1; hρ; sq_le_sq₀; hr; field_simp; ring; nlinarith"
        },
        {
          "title": "Keep the operator-root boundary explicit",
          "text": "The consumer proves a squared B lower bound in a Test module for all true centered macro inputs. It does not construct the positive real-Hilbert root Γ=(B*B)^(1/2), a centered inverse, source weak-H1 equivalence, half-turn mixing, implementation errors or oracle cost.",
          "formula": "\\text{Squared defect bound}\\quad\\not\\Rightarrow\\quad\\text{an already constructed }\\Gamma^{-1}.",
          "lean": "No Gamma/root/inverse declaration is present."
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero as an explicit extension of the source Euclidean setting. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and βη≤1. Set μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd. Let P be the actual conditional-expectation orthogonal projection onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra in L²(J). There exists one linear isometry U:L²(J)→L²(J) whose AE representative is composition with F(x,y)=(x,2x−y), with U²=I and U self-adjoint. Define A=PUP and B=(I−P)UP. For every f∈ran P with ∫f dJ=0, ‖Af‖≤[(1−αη)/(1+αη)]‖f‖ and [4αη/(1+αη)²]‖f‖²≤‖Bf‖². This includes αη=1, uses the actual, potentially infinite-dimensional L²(J), without imposing finite-dimensionality on L², and is Test-level integration of already produced operators; Γ, its inverse and trajectories are not asserted.",
      "lean_proof": "Match the actual previously produced operators; Lift scalar contraction to every macro input; Derive the sharp squared defect gap; Keep the operator-root boundary explicit",
